            <div id="cite-apa" class="tab selected" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-0" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_apa rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_apa rendering_contributiontojournal_apa">Liu, Y., Wang, J., Gao, Q., Pan, M.<a rel="Person" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/persons/yugufang/" class="link"><span>, &amp; Fang, Y.</span></a> (2025). <a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/publications/robust-device-free-mmwave-sensing-with-specular-reflection-interf/" class="link"><span>Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation</span></a>. <a rel="Journal" href="#" class="link"><span><em>IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</em></span></a>, <em>24</em>(7), 5749-5764. <a onclick="window.open(this.href, '_blank','noopener,noreferrer'); return false;" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112" class="link"><span>https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112</span></a></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-author" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-1" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_author rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_author rendering_contributiontojournal_author">Liu, Yulin ; Wang, Jie ; Gao, Qinghua et al. / <a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/publications/robust-device-free-mmwave-sensing-with-specular-reflection-interf/" class="link"><span><strong>Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation</strong></span></a>. In: <a rel="Journal" href="#" class="link"><span>IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</span></a>. 2025 ; Vol. 24, No. 7. pp. 5749-5764.</div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-BIBTEX" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-2" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_bibtex rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_bibtex rendering_contributiontojournal_bibtex"><div>@article{463c6065adfa408fa52b460785ff4591,</div><div>  title     = "Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation",</div><div>  abstract  = "Device-Free mmWave Sensing (DFWS) could sense target state by analyzing how target activities influence the surrounding mmWave signals. It has emerged as a promising sensing technology. However, when employing DFWS indoors, specular reflection interference arises due to the specular reflectors. This interference often induces ghost targets, impacting the accurate estimation of the number and position of targets, resulting in degradation in sensing performance. To tackle this issue, we delve into the generation mechanism of specular reflection interference and analyze its multi-domain characteristics. Through exploration, we discern its temporal sparsity, spatial symmetry or collinearity, and frequency correlation characteristics, and propose four metrics to measure them, accordingly. Specifically, we propose a temporal characteristic quantitative evaluation metric based on identity matching, spatial symmetry and collinearity quantitative evaluation metrics based on geometric analysis, and a frequency correlation quantitative evaluation metric based on Doppler velocity correction, respectively. Based on these metrics, we design a novel Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation (SRIM) method and develop a robust SRIM-DFWS prototype system based on a 60 GHz mmWave radar to validate our proposed method. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed method could achieve accurate and effective mitigation of specular reflection interference in device-free target tracking. {\textcopyright} 2025 IEEE.",</div><div>  keywords  = "Device-free, MmWave sensing, multi-domain characteristics, specular reflection interference",</div><div>  author    = "Yulin Liu and Jie Wang and Qinghua Gao and Miao Pan and Yuguang Fang",</div><div>  year      = "2025",</div><div>  month     = jul,</div><div>  doi       = "10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112",</div><div>  language  = "English",</div><div>  volume    = "24",</div><div>  pages     = "5749--5764",</div><div>  journal   = "IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing",</div><div>  issn      = "1536-1233",</div><div>  publisher = "IEEE",</div><div>  number    = "7",</div><p>}</p></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-harvard" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-3" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_harvard rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_harvard rendering_contributiontojournal_harvard">Liu, Y, Wang, J, Gao, Q, Pan, M<a rel="Person" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/persons/yugufang/" class="link"><span> &amp; Fang, Y</span></a> 2025, '<a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/publications/robust-device-free-mmwave-sensing-with-specular-reflection-interf/" class="link harvard_title"><span>Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation</span></a>', <a rel="Journal" href="#" class="link"><span><em>IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</em></span></a>, vol. 24, no. 7, pp. 5749-5764. <a onclick="window.open(this.href, '_blank','noopener,noreferrer'); return false;" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112" class="link"><span>https://doi.org/10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112</span></a></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-standard" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-4" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_standard rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_standard rendering_contributiontojournal_standard"><a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://scholars.cityu.edu.hk/en/publications/robust-device-free-mmwave-sensing-with-specular-reflection-interf/" class="link"><span><strong>Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation.</strong></span></a> / Liu, Yulin; Wang, Jie; Gao, Qinghua et al. <br />In: <a rel="Journal" href="#" class="link"><span>IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</span></a>, Vol. 24, No. 7, 07.2025, p. 5749-5764.<p class="type"><span class="type_family">Research output<span class="type_family_sep">: </span></span><span class="type_classification_parent">Journal Publications and Reviews<span class="type_parent_sep"> › </span></span><span class="type_classification">RGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal</span><span class="type_classification"><span class="type_parent_sep"> › </span>peer-review</span></p></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-RIS" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-5" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_ris rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_ris rendering_contributiontojournal_ris"><p>TY  - JOUR</p><p>T1  - Robust Device-Free Mmwave Sensing with Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation</p><p>AU  - Liu, Yulin</p><p>AU  - Wang, Jie</p><p>AU  - Gao, Qinghua</p><p>AU  - Pan, Miao</p><p>AU  - Fang, Yuguang</p><p>PY  - 2025/7</p><p>Y1  - 2025/7</p><p>N2  - Device-Free mmWave Sensing (DFWS) could sense target state by analyzing how target activities influence the surrounding mmWave signals. It has emerged as a promising sensing technology. However, when employing DFWS indoors, specular reflection interference arises due to the specular reflectors. This interference often induces ghost targets, impacting the accurate estimation of the number and position of targets, resulting in degradation in sensing performance. To tackle this issue, we delve into the generation mechanism of specular reflection interference and analyze its multi-domain characteristics. Through exploration, we discern its temporal sparsity, spatial symmetry or collinearity, and frequency correlation characteristics, and propose four metrics to measure them, accordingly. Specifically, we propose a temporal characteristic quantitative evaluation metric based on identity matching, spatial symmetry and collinearity quantitative evaluation metrics based on geometric analysis, and a frequency correlation quantitative evaluation metric based on Doppler velocity correction, respectively. Based on these metrics, we design a novel Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation (SRIM) method and develop a robust SRIM-DFWS prototype system based on a 60 GHz mmWave radar to validate our proposed method. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed method could achieve accurate and effective mitigation of specular reflection interference in device-free target tracking.  © 2025 IEEE.</p><p>AB  - Device-Free mmWave Sensing (DFWS) could sense target state by analyzing how target activities influence the surrounding mmWave signals. It has emerged as a promising sensing technology. However, when employing DFWS indoors, specular reflection interference arises due to the specular reflectors. This interference often induces ghost targets, impacting the accurate estimation of the number and position of targets, resulting in degradation in sensing performance. To tackle this issue, we delve into the generation mechanism of specular reflection interference and analyze its multi-domain characteristics. Through exploration, we discern its temporal sparsity, spatial symmetry or collinearity, and frequency correlation characteristics, and propose four metrics to measure them, accordingly. Specifically, we propose a temporal characteristic quantitative evaluation metric based on identity matching, spatial symmetry and collinearity quantitative evaluation metrics based on geometric analysis, and a frequency correlation quantitative evaluation metric based on Doppler velocity correction, respectively. Based on these metrics, we design a novel Specular Reflection Interference Mitigation (SRIM) method and develop a robust SRIM-DFWS prototype system based on a 60 GHz mmWave radar to validate our proposed method. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed method could achieve accurate and effective mitigation of specular reflection interference in device-free target tracking.  © 2025 IEEE.</p><p>KW  - Device-free</p><p>KW  - MmWave sensing</p><p>KW  - multi-domain characteristics</p><p>KW  - specular reflection interference</p><p>UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217532407</p><p>UR  - https://www.scopus.com/record/pubmetrics.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85217532407&amp;origin=recordpage</p><p>U2  - 10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112</p><p>DO  - 10.1109/TMC.2025.3538112</p><p>M3  - RGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal</p><p>SN  - 1536-1233</p><p>VL  - 24</p><p>SP  - 5749</p><p>EP  - 5764</p><p>JO  - IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</p><p>JF  - IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing</p><p>IS  - 7</p><p>ER  - </p></div>
            </div>
        
